>> title: Crema Mexicana
>> category: Dressings & Dips
>> tags: cream, cultured, mexican, condiment, make-ahead
>> counters: Panadería, Taquería
>> aka: crema, mexican crema, mexican sour cream, crema agria, table cream
>> pairs-with: birria-de-res, refried-beans
>> servings: 12
>> time: 28 hr 15 min
>> step.1: warm to 85°F (29°C)
>> step.2: whisk in the buttermilk, culture 24 hr
>> step.3: stir in the lime and salt
>> step.4: chill 4 hr

Warm @heavy cream{2%cup}(480 mL) and @whole milk{1/2%cup}(120 mL) in a #saucepan{} to 85°F (29°C), which is barely warm to a finger. Hotter than 110°F and the culture dies.

Whisk @cultured buttermilk{1/2%cup}(120 mL) into @&(~1)warm cream{}, cover the pan with a cloth, and leave it on the counter to culture ~ferment{24%hr}, until it coats a spoon and smells faintly sour.

Stir @lime juice{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @lime zest{1/2%tsp}(from 1 lime) and @fine sea salt{1/2%tsp} into @&(~1)cultured cream{}. Mexican crema is pourable and lightly salted, which is what separates it from sour cream.

Refrigerate @&(~1)crema{} ~chill{4%hr} to set; it thickens as it cools and keeps 2 weeks.
